      ":question/id": "9392ab96-5be3-5aab-8c35-808d0b88162a",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-37384",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to ${Q}^{-}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that ${Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $1$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\sqrt{18}=-3\\sqrt{2}$ is a not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $\\sqrt{6}$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $0$ is not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None of those listed\"."
